		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Voice prompts update]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2472&amp;p=20493#p20493"><![CDATA[
The voice prompts have been updated to support the GPS screen in the MD-UV380 / RT-3S<br><br>The latest voice prompts are now located in <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest" class="postlink">downloads/Voice_Prompts/Latest</a><br><br>The latest wordlist files are available from the localisation folder <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/localisation/voice_prompt_texts/" class="postlink">downloads/localisation/voice_prompt_texts/</a><br><br><br><strong class="text-strong">For anyone who wants to build their own version the voice prompt files</strong><br><br>The voice prompt creation Python script is located in   <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/tools" class="postlink">downloads/Voice_Prompts/tools</a><br>The other configuation files needed to build the voice promptscan be downloaded from <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/Voice_Prompts/data" class="postlink">downloads/Voice_Prompts/data</a> <br>The languages.zip file need to be unzipped into the build folder, and creates the necessary file structure including all existing mp3 files<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Nov 02, 2022 8:48 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
